---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";

const basePath = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Frequently asked questions"
  description="Answers about what Veasel Code can do today, model providers, local data, the V language mascot, and contributing."
>
  <section class="doc-page page-grid">
    <p class="kicker">FIELD GUIDE / COMMON QUESTIONS</p>
    <h1>
      Clear answers.
      <br />
      <em>Room to grow.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Veasel Code is being built in public. Here is what the current source
      build does, what it does not do yet, and where to follow changes.
    </p>
    <div class="doc-panel faq-panel">
      <h2>Can Veasel Code change files in my repository?</h2>
      <p>
        It can propose a bounded edit to one text file at a time. In the TUI,
        inspect the saved diff with <code>/patch show &lt;id&gt;</code> and
        explicitly approve it with <code>/patch approve &lt;id&gt;</code>. The
        loopback API has no application token, so same-user processes can call
        its review and approval routes. Veasel can also propose shell commands;
        each one must be opened and approved with its exact command, working
        directory, and timeout. Approved commands run with the server user's
        permissions and without an OS sandbox.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-panel faq-panel">
      <h2>Does my code stay on my machine?</h2>
      <p>
        Session history is stored in a local SQLite database managed by the
        Veasel Code backend. Prompts and recent conversation context are sent to
        the model provider you configure. If the model requests workspace tools,
        the matching file excerpts and tool results are sent to that provider
        too.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-panel faq-panel">
      <h2>How do I find a session when the home list is long?</h2>
      <p>
        The home sidebar keeps the selected session on screen. Press
        <kbd>j</kbd> or <kbd>k</kbd>, or the arrow keys, to move, then Enter to
        open it. When the list is taller than the terminal, Veasel shows a
        position such as <code>8/20</code> and omits sessions outside that
        window. Long titles are clipped from the front and long directories from
        the end, so the workspace name stays visible. A list that fits shows
        every session and no position counter. Press <kbd>n</kbd> to start a
        session when the list is empty.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-panel faq-panel">
      <h2>What happens if an async turn is interrupted?</h2>
      <p>
        Async session turns have a durable operation ID and status you can query
        after reconnecting. If the server stops before storing a result, Veasel
        marks the turn <code>uncertain</code> and never retries a provider call
        or possible tool effect automatically. Inspect your workspace and
        operation status before deciding whether to try again. Durable queued
        workers remain in development.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-panel faq-panel">
      <h2>Which AI providers can I use?</h2>
      <p>
        The V backend supports OpenAI Chat Completions and Responses, Meta Model
        API Responses, Anthropic Messages, Gemini, and many OpenAI-compatible
        endpoints. These are four protocol families, not independent native
        adapters for every preset. See{" "}
        <a href={`${basePath}/docs/providers/`}>provider setup</a> and data
        disclosure details.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-panel faq-panel">
      <h2>How much text can one message contain?</h2>
      <p>
        A submitted conversation is limited to 1 MiB (1,048,576 bytes) of text.
        That limit is not a model's token window. Veasel does not yet use Muse's
        advertised 1,048,576-token context window. The output-token budget is
        filled in when you choose a model; press <kbd>Ctrl+O</kbd> to change it.
        Zero keeps Veasel's 4,096-token default, except Meta, which leaves the
        field unset so Meta applies its own limit.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-panel faq-panel">
      <h2>Can I use Agent Plugins already?</h2>
      <p>
        Support is experimental. Veasel discovers local packages, lets you
        enable validated Skill instructions per session, and can expose trusted
        stdio or Streamable HTTP MCP servers as model tools. Use
        <code>/mcp</code> and <code>/mcp trust plugin/server</code> to trust a
        server for the session. Trust permits a server to connect; each
        model-requested tool call pauses the turn until you inspect its exact
        arguments with <code>/mcp calls</code> and approve or reject it.
        Rejected calls are not retried. Trusted stdio processes run with the
        server user's permissions and have no OS sandbox. Veasel does not
        install plugins or claim full Agent Plugins compatibility.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-panel faq-panel">
      <h2>Why is the terminal client TypeScript?</h2>
      <p>
        The TUI uses OpenTUI for terminal rendering and talks to a versioned
        API. The server, agent runtime, and persistence are V; the client
        remains a separate API consumer.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-panel faq-panel">
      <h2>Can I use the Veasel mascot commercially?</h2>
      <p>
        The official mascot and this pixel adaptation are under CC BY-NC 4.0.
        Commercial use needs separate permission from the rights holder.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-panel faq-panel">
      <h2>How do I follow the project or contribute?</h2>
      <p>
        Read the <a href={`${basePath}/docs/roadmap/`}>verified roadmap</a>,
        open the repository, and use its issue or pull request templates to
        propose focused work.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="doc-next">
      <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel">
        Open Veasel Code on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="text-link" href={`${basePath}/docs/`}>
        Back to the field guide <span aria-hidden="true">↑</span>
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
